    ["EN-REA-003","english","Reading","2","เข้าใจ","G-EN-002","Street art was once seen as vandalism. People painted on walls without permission, and city workers quickly covered their work. Today, many cities invite artists to paint large murals on old buildings. In some towns, these murals have become tourist attractions, and local shops earn more money because visitors come to take photos. However, not everyone is happy. Some residents say that the murals change the character of their neighbourhood, and that rents go up when an area becomes popular. City planners now try to ask local people what they want before a new mural is painted.","What is the passage mainly about?","How to paint a mural","How attitudes to street art have changed and the problems it can bring","Why tourists like taking photos","Why rents are high in big cities","","B","บทอ่านเล่าว่าศิลปะบนถนนเคยถูกมองว่าเป็นการทำลาย แต่ตอนนี้เมืองเชิญศิลปินมาวาด และยังมีปัญหาบางอย่าง (ค่าเช่าสูง ชุมชนเปลี่ยนไป)","ไม่มีขั้นตอนการวาด","ถูกต้อง","เป็นเพียงรายละเอียดเล็กๆ","เป็นผลกระทบข้อหนึ่งเท่านั้น","ใจความหลักต้องครอบคลุมทั้งต้น กลาง และท้ายบทอ่าน","","","active","original"],
    ["EN-REA-004","english","Reading","1","จำ","G-EN-002","","According to the passage, how do local shops benefit from murals?","They earn more money from visitors.","They pay lower rents.","They can sell paint to artists.","They get free paintings.","","A","บทอ่านบอกว่า \"local shops earn more money because visitors come to take photos\"","ถูกต้อง","บทอ่านบอกว่าค่าเช่าสูงขึ้น ไม่ใช่ลดลง","ไม่มีในบทอ่าน","ไม่มีในบทอ่าน","ข้อถามรายละเอียด หาคำสำคัญ (shops) แล้วอ่านประโยครอบๆ","","","active","original"],
    ["EN-REA-005","english","Reading","2","เข้าใจ","G-EN-002","","The word \"vandalism\" in the first sentence is closest in meaning to ______.","a job in the city","a type of tourism","damaging property on purpose","a famous kind of painting","","C","ประโยคถัดมาบอกว่าวาดโดยไม่ได้รับอนุญาตและถูกลบทิ้ง แสดงว่าเป็นการทำลายทรัพย์สิน","ไม่ใช่อาชีพ","ไม่เกี่ยวกับการท่องเที่ยว","ถูกต้อง","ขัดกับการถูกลบทิ้ง","เดาความหมายคำจากประโยคข้างเคียง (context clues)","","","active","original"],
    ["EN-REA-006","english","Reading","3","วิเคราะห์","G-EN-002","","What can be inferred about city planners today?","They only care about tourists.","They want to stop all street art.","They think residents' opinions are important.","They paint the murals themselves.","","C","ประโยคสุดท้ายบอกว่าพวกเขาถามคนในพื้นที่ก่อนวาด แสดงว่าให้ความสำคัญกับความเห็นของผู้อยู่อาศัย","ขัดกับการถามคนในพื้นที่","บทอ่านไม่ได้บอกว่าจะหยุด","ถูกต้อง","บทอ่านไม่ได้บอก","ข้ออนุมาน (infer) คำตอบไม่ได้เขียนตรงๆ แต่ต้องมีหลักฐานในบทอ่าน","","","active","original"],
    ["EN-REA-007","english","Reading","1","จำ","G-EN-003","Kanya started drawing comics when she was nine. At first she copied characters from her favourite books, but her art teacher encouraged her to create her own. \"Copying is a good way to learn,\" the teacher said, \"but your own stories are more interesting.\" Kanya began carrying a small notebook everywhere. She sketched people on the bus, cats in the market and the faces of her classmates. Two years later, she won a regional comic competition with a story about a girl who can talk to street dogs. Now she posts a short comic online every week, and more than ten thousand people follow her.","How did Kanya start drawing comics?","She took a comic course.","She copied characters from books.","She drew street dogs.","She followed artists online.","","B","บทอ่านบอกว่า \"At first she copied characters from her favourite books\"","ไม่มีในบทอ่าน","ถูกต้อง","เป็นเรื่องในการ์ตูนที่ชนะการประกวดภายหลัง","ไม่มีในบทอ่าน","คำว่า At first บอกจุดเริ่มต้นของเรื่อง","","","active","original"],
    ["EN-REA-008","english","Reading","2","เข้าใจ","G-EN-003","","What was the teacher's advice?","Copying helps you learn, but creating your own stories is better.","Draw only animals.","Post comics online every day.","Stop copying and never look at other comics.","","A","ครูพูดว่า copying is a good way to learn แต่ your own stories are more interesting","ถูกต้อง","ไม่มีในบทอ่าน","ไม่ใช่คำแนะนำของครู","ครูไม่ได้ห้ามลอก บอกว่าลอกช่วยให้เรียนรู้","อ่านคำพูดในเครื่องหมายคำพูดให้ครบทั้งสองส่วน","","","active","original"],
