    ["EN-REA-011","english","Reading","1","จำ","G-EN-004","Colour can change the way we feel. Studies show that warm colours such as red and orange can make people feel energetic, while cool colours such as blue and green often make them feel calm. This is why many fast-food restaurants use red and yellow in their logos and interiors: these colours attract attention and may even make customers eat faster. Hospitals, on the other hand, often choose soft blues and greens to help patients relax. Designers must remember, however, that the meaning of colour also depends on culture. White is worn at weddings in some countries but is a colour of mourning in others.","According to the passage, which colours can make people feel calm?","white and black","red and orange","blue and green","red and yellow","","C","\"cool colours such as blue and green often make them feel calm\"","ไม่ได้กล่าวว่าทำให้สงบ","เป็นสีโทนร้อน ให้ความรู้สึกกระตือรือร้น","ถูกต้อง","สีของร้านอาหารจานด่วน","warm colours = energetic · cool colours = calm","","","active","original"],
    ["EN-REA-012","english","Reading","2","เข้าใจ","G-EN-004","","Why do many fast-food restaurants use red and yellow?","They are cheap colours.","They attract attention and may make people eat faster.","They help customers relax.","They are the colours of mourning.","","B","บทอ่านบอกว่าสีเหล่านี้ \"attract attention and may even make customers eat faster\"","ไม่มีในบทอ่าน","ถูกต้อง","เป็นผลของสีโทนเย็นในโรงพยาบาล","ไม่ได้กล่าวถึงสีแดง/เหลือง","อ่านประโยคที่มีคำว่า This is why … เพื่อหาเหตุผล","","","active","original"],
    ["EN-REA-013","english","Reading","2","เข้าใจ","G-EN-004","","The phrase \"on the other hand\" is used to ______.","show a contrast","add a similar idea","give a conclusion","give an example","","A","ประโยคก่อนพูดถึงร้านอาหาร (กระตุ้น) ประโยคหลังพูดถึงโรงพยาบาล (ผ่อนคลาย) = เปรียบเทียบความต่าง","ถูกต้อง","เพิ่มเติมใช้ also / moreover","สรุปใช้ in conclusion","ตัวอย่างใช้ for example","on the other hand = ในทางกลับกัน (แสดงความต่าง)","","","active","original"],
    ["EN-REA-014","english","Reading","3","วิเคราะห์","G-EN-004","","What is the main point of the last two sentences?","Colours have the same meaning everywhere.","Mourning clothes must be black.","White is the best wedding colour.","Designers should think about culture when choosing colours.","","D","ผู้เขียนเตือนว่าความหมายของสีขึ้นกับวัฒนธรรม และยกตัวอย่างสีขาว","ขัดกับบทอ่าน","บทอ่านไม่ได้พูดถึงสีดำ","ไม่ได้บอกว่าดีที่สุด","ถูกต้อง","however มักนำประเด็นสำคัญที่ผู้เขียนต้องการเน้น","","","active","original"],
    ["EN-REA-015","english","Reading","1","จำ","G-EN-005","The school recycling project began with a simple question from a Grade 8 student: \"Why do we throw away so much paper?\" A group of students counted the paper in the school bins for one week and found more than 300 kilograms. They presented their results at the morning assembly and suggested three changes. First, every classroom would have a separate box for paper. Second, students would print on both sides. Third, scrap paper would be collected for the art department. After one term, the amount of wasted paper fell by half, and the art teachers said they had never had so much free paper for sketching.","How much paper did the students find in one week?","3,000 kilograms","about 30 kilograms","more than 300 kilograms","half a kilogram","","C","\"found more than 300 kilograms\"","ตัวเลขผิด","ตัวเลขผิด","ถูกต้อง","ตัวเลขผิด","ข้อถามตัวเลข อ่านให้ตรงหน่วยและคำขยาย (more than)","","","active","original"],
    ["EN-REA-016","english","Reading","2","เข้าใจ","G-EN-005","","Which was NOT one of the students' suggestions?","a paper box in every classroom","printing on both sides","giving scrap paper to the art department","buying cheaper paper","","D","ข้อเสนอสามข้อคือ กล่องแยกกระดาษ พิมพ์สองหน้า และเก็บกระดาษเหลือให้แผนกศิลปะ ไม่มีการซื้อกระดาษถูกลง","เป็นข้อเสนอที่ 1","เป็นข้อเสนอที่ 2","เป็นข้อเสนอที่ 3","ถูกต้อง","ข้อที่มี NOT ให้ตัดตัวเลือกที่พบในบทอ่านออกทีละข้อ","","","active","original"],
    ["EN-REA-017","english","Reading","2","เข้าใจ","G-EN-005","","What happened after one term?","Wasted paper was reduced by 50%.","The art department closed.","Students stopped printing.","The school stopped using paper.","","A","\"the amount of wasted paper fell by half\" = ลดลงครึ่งหนึ่ง (50%)","ถูกต้อง","ไม่มีในบทอ่าน","ไม่มีในบทอ่าน","ไม่มีในบทอ่าน","fell by half = ลดลงครึ่งหนึ่ง","","","active","original"],
    ["EN-REA-018","english","Reading","3","วิเคราะห์","G-EN-005","","What lesson does the passage mainly teach?","Recycling is too difficult for schools.","Assemblies are boring.","Art teachers need more paper.","One question from a student can lead to real change.","","D","โครงการเริ่มจากคำถามของนักเรียนคนเดียว และจบด้วยการลดขยะได้จริง","ขัดกับผลลัพธ์ที่ทำได้จริง","ไม่มีในบทอ่าน","เป็นเพียงผลพลอยได้","ถูกต้อง","ข้อถามบทเรียน ให้ดูว่าเรื่องเริ่มจากอะไรและจบอย่างไร","","","active","original"],
    ["EN-REA-019","english","Reading","1","จำ","G-EN-006","Before the invention of photography in the 19th century, the only way to record what a person looked like was to paint or draw a portrait. Rich families paid artists to paint them, and these portraits were often hung in large halls to show the family's power. When cameras became cheaper, many people thought painting would disappear. Instead, painters began to explore things a camera could not do. Some, like the Impressionists, painted the changing effects of light. Others used strange colours and shapes to express feelings. In this way, photography actually pushed painting in new directions.","Before photography, how could people record what someone looked like?","by using a camera","by writing a letter","by painting or drawing a portrait","by making a video","","C","ประโยคแรก: \"the only way … was to paint or draw a portrait\"","กล้องเกิดขึ้นภายหลัง","ไม่มีในบทอ่าน","ถูกต้อง","ยังไม่มีวิดีโอในยุคนั้น","Before … = ก่อน… ให้สังเกตลำดับเวลา","","","active","original"],
