    ["EN-REA-026","english","Reading","2","วิเคราะห์","G-EN-007","","Why should students apply early?","Only 30 places are available.","The designer is leaving.","Lunch is limited.","The workshop is expensive.","","A","\"places are limited to 30 students\" ถ้าสมัครช้าอาจไม่ได้ที่","ถูกต้อง","ไม่มีในประกาศ","ไม่มีในประกาศ","ฟรี","limited = มีจำกัด → ควรรีบ","","","active","original"],
    ["EN-REA-027","english","Reading","1","จำ","G-EN-008","Thai lacquerware is a traditional craft that has been practised for hundreds of years. Craftspeople first make a base from bamboo or wood. They then cover it with many thin layers of lacquer, a natural resin from a tree. Each layer must dry completely before the next one is added, so a single piece can take several months to finish. Some pieces are decorated with gold leaf or with tiny pieces of shell. Because the process is slow and difficult, fewer young people want to learn it today. Several communities in northern Thailand now run classes for teenagers to keep the skill alive.","What is lacquer, according to the passage?","gold leaf","a type of shell","a kind of bamboo","a natural resin from a tree","","D","\"lacquer, a natural resin from a tree\" (คำอธิบายหลังจุลภาค)","เป็นวัสดุตกแต่ง","เป็นวัสดุตกแต่ง","ไม้ไผ่เป็นโครงฐาน","ถูกต้อง","คำนิยามมักอยู่หลังจุลภาค (appositive)","","","active","original"],
